Z||000000||ZeroFiero||12-06-2001||01:29 AM||||Hey all... I like the forum... very nice.<BR>I'm new to fiero's... If I recall, spaceframe, merd, 4 wheel independent susp.? <BR>approx 2800 lbs. curb weight... 0.83 g '85GT<BR>lat accel.? correct me where I'm wrong, please. I did a search but couldn't find<BR>this. Sorry for the silly questions.<P>Now then, come spring when I out<BR>of school and hopefully have a full-time<BR>job, I want to get a fiero for a project<BR>car. I was thinking 250 HP net, 1.00g lat <BR>accel, light as possible, and maybe 25 mpg.<BR>So perhaps a 3.4L swap... 3800sc is hard to<BR>come by here... maybe manage a 3800T, but <BR>probably harder to do, I think that's a RWD<BR>engine... <P>Anyway... I know of three fieros for sale<BR>84SE... supposedly perfect running<BR>condition, gas tank and fuel pump not <BR>installed but with car, black, $530 US firm<P>85 base, 5spd? red, perfect chassis, one<BR>inch rip in side of seat, otherwise<BR>perfect... 4cyl almost dead (faulty rod, I think) $300 US maybe haggle.<P>86 or 87 fastback 6cyl auto, gold<BR>broken trunk lid, cracked front clip.<BR>6 cyl is blown, no seats $530 US.<P>Which one is best, and why? how hard<BR>is it to get panels for the 86, and<BR>seats?<P>There is an amazing amount of firebirds<BR>in the junkyards here. Which parts should<BR>I take?<P>Thanks,<BR>ZeroFiero<P>Again, My compliments on the great forum.<P>P.S. I can figure out how to fabricate brackets, etc for the engine swap.<BR>Fairly good/can learn all the mechanic<BR>work necessary.||||reg||7
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||12-06-2001||06:33 AM||||Welcome to the Forum.  My advise is to get the Fiero which has the best parts for your needs.  I would lean towards the least rust possible, personally.  <P>Also the 84 will need wiring changes to go V6 or better. The other two boil down to your preference between coupe and fastback.<P>The fastback commands slightly more $$$.  Body parts are easily replaced as are seats. Fastback 1/4 windows are pricey.<P>I would lean toward the 85 coupe myself as I've been down the 'rust road' and it ain't no fun.<P>Where are you in Canada? Lots of us Canucks are here.<BR>Gary<BR>86 GT<BR>86 SE times two||||reg||6
Z||000002||Jay||12-06-2001||08:26 AM||||Welcome to the forum.  I also would lean towards the 6 cyl cars.  I'm partial to the GT's but it boils down to preference.  If it were me I'd take the GT's even though they are auto.  Lot's of parts available for all of them.  Try "Race-Tech the Fiero shop" in Toronto.  They got lots of project cars sitting out front waiting for a new owner.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever3000||12-06-2001||09:48 AM||||Welcome!<BR>If these are your choices (meaning you've already looked in our Mall section here), go for the 85.  The other two sound like the prices are a little high for what you're getting.  And if you will be swapping the engine soon, that tired 4 cylinder doesn't matter.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cheever_gold_sig.jpg"> <BR><I>Try to keep up!</I>||||reg||6
Z||000004||ZeroFiero||12-06-2001||12:06 PM||||Thanks Guys.<P>I'm from Fort St. John, B.C.<BR>The main pronlem with getting things from<BR>the mall is distance. (I'm just outside <BR>the Yukon, for those who don't know where <BR>Fort St. John is.) If I buy something <BR>from toronto which I can't drive here,<BR>it'll cost a grand to get it here...<BR>same from almost anywhere else... so<BR>I'm limited to local choices.<BR>I can probably haggle the 86 fastback down...<BR>It's in a junkyard, and the owner is retiring<BR>and crushing everything.. (arg... nice stuff in there.) prob is its auto... I thought<BR>I read about needing the 2.8L manifolds and<BR>various engine attachments to swap in certain<BR>v6s. How hard to convert a notchback to a<BR>fastback? more important... is it actually<BR>more aerodynamic?<P>Thanks<BR>ZeroFiero<P>The mall is cool... probably get small parts<BR>from there.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
